MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Your inbox was the database. persistRecord() no-ops entirely without Upstash,
and /api/health reported durableKv:false on the live deployment — so a paid
order existed in exactly two places, Stripe and one email. No list of open
orders, no record of what had been fulfilled, and a dropped Resend message made
an order invisible. You cannot run a paid funnel you cannot enumerate.

This is the P1 minimal CRM — Lead, Project, Stage, Owner, Next Action, Value,
Source — built as a state machine rather than a table.

- shared/ledger.ts (new): seven stages with VALIDATED transitions. An order
  cannot jump paid → delivered without passing through the work, and refunded
  is genuinely terminal. Every accepted move appends to the record's own audit
  history, so "who moved this and when" never depends on memory.
- Next Action is DERIVED, never stored: computed from stage, age and the tier's
  fulfillment spec. A next action someone must remember to update is one that
  goes stale in a week. An order sitting in awaiting_data past 7 days reports
  "Seit N Tagen keine Projektdaten — nachfassen bei <email>" on its own.
- server/kv.ts (new): the Upstash accessor extracted from index.ts so the
  ledger can use it without importing the Express app.
- server/ledger-store.ts (new): Redis hash + sorted index, keyed on the human
  reference (ET-XXXXXXXX) rather than the session id — a ledger keyed on
  something nobody can read aloud is a ledger nobody uses. Writes return
  { durable } and NEVER silently succeed; without a store the webhook logs
  "[ledger] NO DURABLE STORE" and stamps a warning banner into the operator
  email instead of losing the order quietly.
- The webhook now creates the ledger record, advances intake → paid, and — once
  the customer confirmation is actually delivered — advances paid →
  awaiting_data. The stage tracks reality without anyone updating it.
- GET /api/admin/orders: worklist sorted overdue-first then oldest, with a
  summary (open count, overdue count, open value in cents, non-durable count).
  Optional ?stage= filter.
- POST /api/admin/orders/:reference/stage: advance a stage, optionally claim an
  owner and leave a note. A rejected transition returns 409 WITH the list of
  allowed stages — a refusal that tells you what you can do instead.
- Admin auth is a constant-time compare against ADMIN_API_TOKEN (a plain ===
  leaks the prefix through timing). Under 16 chars the surface is disabled
  entirely rather than weakly protected. Audit entries carry a sha256 prefix of
  the token, never the token.
- /api/health gains durableOrders and adminApi. smoke-test.sh asserts 401 on
  both admin routes with no token and with a wrong token, and warns loudly when
  the ledger is not durable.
- scripts/dev-kv.mjs + `pnpm dev:kv`: a dev-only in-memory Upstash-REST stand-in
  so this can be exercised locally without provisioning anything.

Evidence: pnpm check clean, 96/96 vitest (21 new), pnpm build clean.
Live against dev-kv: 401 with no token, 401 with a wrong token, 200 with the
right one; four seeded orders render a correct worklist (open=3, overdue=1,
open value 6.970,00 EUR); awaiting_data → delivered rejected 409 with
allowed:[in_progress,refunded,closed]; awaiting_data → in_progress accepted and
the owner persisted. smoke-test 18/18 configured, 16/16 unconfigured.

